{"meta":{"engine":"This is LuaHBTeX, Version 1.21.0 (TeX Live 2025)","format":"lualatex"},"params":{"textwidth":23592960,"textheight":35481206,"topskip":[720896,0,0,0,0],"parskip":[0,65536,0,0,0],"parindent":1114112,"baselineskip":[891290,0,0,0,0],"oddsidemargin":3538944,"topmargin":1376256,"headheight":786432,"headsep":1638400,"footskip":1966080,"maxdepth":360448,"widowpenalty":150,"clubpenalty":150},"pages":[{"number":1,"pagewidth":40258437,"pageheight":52099153,"lines":[{"x":8275230,"y":12135300,"w":23592960,"h":798386,"d":233287,"text":" Notes on Keeping a Small Vegetable Garden "},{"x":16737632,"y":14129232,"w":6668157,"h":642250,"d":275254,"text":" Marguerite Odell "},{"x":8275230,"y":15738141,"w":23592960,"h":545784,"d":151781,"text":" March 3, 2024 "},{"x":8275230,"y":18281352,"w":23592960,"h":457441,"d":3932,"text":" Abstract "},{"x":10069277,"y":19420456,"w":20004866,"h":454820,"d":135004,"text":" This short note collects practical observations about planning, plant-"},{"x":10069277,"y":20206888,"w":20004866,"h":462029,"d":135004,"text":"ing and maintaining a vegetable garden of modest size. It is written"},{"x":10069277,"y":20993320,"w":20004866,"h":462029,"d":135004,"text":"for beginners who have a sunny corner, a few tools and a considerable"},{"x":10069277,"y":21779752,"w":20004866,"h":462029,"d":7209,"text":"amount of enthusiasm. "},{"x":8275230,"y":24025241,"w":23592960,"h":654940,"d":189687,"text":"1 Planning the Beds "},{"x":8275230,"y":25627908,"w":23592960,"h":513815,"d":147830,"text":"A garden begins on paper. Before any soil is turned, it is worth walking the"},{"x":8275230,"y":26519198,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147830,"text":"site at different hours of the day and noting where the shadows fall. Most"},{"x":8275230,"y":27410488,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147830,"text":"vegetables need at least six hours of direct sunlight, and tomatoes, peppers"},{"x":8275230,"y":28301778,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147830,"text":"and squash greatly prefer more. "},{"x":8275230,"y":30207800,"w":23592960,"h":548143,"d":158073,"text":"1.1 Choosing a Location "},{"x":8275230,"y":31563031,"w":23592960,"h":498028,"d":147830,"text":"Level ground is convenient, but it is not essential. Water drains poorly in"},{"x":8275230,"y":32454321,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147112,"text":"hollows, so an apparently ideal flat patch may turn into a swamp after the"},{"x":8275230,"y":33345611,"w":23592960,"h":609594,"d":147112,"text":"first heavy rain.1 "},{"x":8275230,"y":35251632,"w":23592960,"h":548930,"d":8651,"text":"A Word on Soil "},{"x":8275230,"y":36606863,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147112,"text":"Good soil is dark, crumbly and smells faintly sweet. Compost improves"},{"x":8275230,"y":37498153,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147112,"text":"almost every kind of soil, whether sandy or heavy with clay. "},{"x":8275230,"y":39743643,"w":23592960,"h":654940,"d":7550,"text":"2 What to Plant "},{"x":8275230,"y":41346310,"w":23592960,"h":505921,"d":147830,"text":"The following crops are forgiving and productive: "},{"x":10069277,"y":42739023,"w":21798913,"h":498028,"d":147112,"text":" • Radishes, which are ready in about a month. "},{"x":8275230,"y":44018580,"w":23592960,"h":512445,"d":216271,"text":" 1A simple test is to dig a hole, fill it with water, and measure how long it takes to empty. "},{"x":8275230,"y":45984660,"w":23592960,"h":477934,"d":0,"text":" 1 "}],"rules":[[8275230,43309527,9437040,26214]],"body":{"width":23592960,"height":35481206,"depth":0,"glueSign":2,"glueOrder":0,"glueSet":0.269776732,"items":[["o","whatsit"],["glue",720896,0,0,0,0,10],["h",0,0,0,0,""],["glue",1435238,0,0,0,0,0],["glue",-1435238,0,0,0,0,0],["p",-51],["glue",1435238,0,0,0,0,0],["glue",0,65536,0,0,0,3],["glue",0,0,0,0,0,3],["glue",643406,0,0,0,0,2],["h",23592960,798386,233287,0," Notes on Keeping a Small Vegetable Garden "],["glue",1076428,0,0,0,0,0],["glue",0,65536,0,0,0,3],["glue",0,0,0,0,0,3],["glue",41967,0,0,0,0,2],["h",23592960,642250,275254,0," Mar